### Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| `ParseError` with `field` + `received` | Pinpoints exactly what failed and what value was given |
| `timestamp` accepts `Date`, `string`, or `number` | Handles real-world inputs (API JSON, DB records, in-memory objects) |
| `JsonValue` recursive type for payload | Ensures payload is always serializable; rejects `undefined`, functions, `Symbol` |
| `name.trim()` applied on output | Normalizes whitespace while still rejecting blank strings |
| Type guards (`isRecord`, `isJsonValue`) | Keeps the main function clean and makes guards reusable |

