## Breakdown

### `RequestOptions` Interface
| Property  | Type                                                          | Required | Description                          |
|-----------|---------------------------------------------------------------|----------|--------------------------------------|
| `method`  | `"GET" \| "POST" \| "PUT" \| "PATCH" \| "DELETE" \| ...`    | ✅ Yes   | HTTP method (union type for safety)  |
| `url`     | `string`                                                      | ✅ Yes   | Target URL                           |
| `headers` | `Record<string, string>`                                      | ❌ No    | Key-value pairs for request headers  |
| `body`    | `BodyInit \| null`                                            | ❌ No    | Request body (string, FormData, etc.)|

### Key Implementation Details

- **URL Validation** — Uses the `URL` constructor to validate the URL before making the request, throwing a descriptive error if invalid
- **Body Restriction** — Automatically omits the body for `GET` and `HEAD` requests, as per the HTTP spec
- **Error Handling** — Checks `response.ok` (status 200–299) and throws a descriptive error for failed requests
- **`BodyInit` type** — Accepts `string`, `Blob`, `FormData`, `URLSearchParams`, `ArrayBuffer`, or `ReadableStream` as the body

